tick: 338
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I will implement a \"Multiple Restarts\" local search strategy. This will involve running the local search 5 times, each starting from the baseline configuration with a small random offset. Each local search will run for 5000 steps with a `perturbation_strength` of 0.018. The best result across all 5 runs will be returned.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Multiple Restarts Local Search on Baseline Centers\"\ntags: \"local search, multiple restarts, baseline improvement, ensemble optimization\"\nabstract: \"This submission implements a 'multiple restarts' strategy for the local search algorithm. It performs 5 independent local search runs, each initialized with the System's 'Ring Pattern Baseline' configuration, but with a small random initial offset applied to all centers to introduce variation. Each run uses 5000 perturbation steps and an optimal `perturbation_strength` of 0.018. The best performing configuration across all 5 runs\
    \ is selected as the final result, aiming to find a better global optimum by exploring multiple local optima.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers):\n      \"\"\"\n      Computes the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n      within a unit square, ensuring no overlap.\n      Includes a safety margin for robustness against floating-point errors.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-9 # Used for general small value comparisons and boundary checks\n      safety_margin = 1e-7 # Ensures strict non-overlap for evaluator\n      radii = np.ones(n) # Initialize with large radii, will shrink\n      \n      # Limit by distance to square borders, ensuring a minimum radius\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          radii[i] = min(x - epsilon, y - epsilon, 1 - x - epsilon, 1 - y - epsilon)\n          radii[i] = max(radii[i], epsilon) # Ensure all radii are at least epsilon\n      \n      # Iteratively\
    \ shrink radii to resolve overlaps.\n      # Using 50 iterations for sufficient convergence.\n      for _ in range(50): \n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  \n                  # Check for overlap condition using epsilon\n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon:\n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq)\n                      \n                      # Handle cases where centers are very close or identical\n                      if dist < 2 * epsilon: \n                          radii[i] = epsilon \n                          radii[j] = epsilon\n                      else:\n                          # Target sum of radii is `dist - safety_margin` to guarantee no overlap\n                          target_rad_sum = dist - safety_margin\n                          \n                          # Only scale\
    \ if current sum is greater than the target sum\n                          if rad_sum > target_rad_sum:\n                              scale_factor = target_rad_sum / rad_sum\n                              radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                              radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      \n      return np.maximum(radii, epsilon) # Final check to ensure all radii are positive\n\n  def run_local_search(initial_centers_base, num_steps, perturbation_strength, random_offset_scale):\n      \"\"\"\n      Runs a single local search optimization from a given initial configuration.\n      \"\"\"\n      n_circles = initial_centers_base.shape[0]\n      \n      # Apply a small random offset to the baseline centers for this run\n      initial_centers = np.copy(initial_centers_base)\n      initial_centers += np.random.uniform(-random_offset_scale, random_offset_scale, (n_circles, 2))\n      initial_centers = np.clip(initial_centers, 0.0, 1.0) # Ensure centers stay within bounds\n      \n     \
    \ # Calculate initial radii and score for this run\n      best_centers_run = initial_centers\n      best_radii_run = compute_max_radii(best_centers_run)\n      best_score_run = np.sum(best_radii_run)\n      \n      # print(f\"  Initial score for this run: {best_score_run:.6f}\") # Too verbose for full log\n      \n      for step in range(num_steps):\n          current_centers = np.copy(best_centers_run)\n          \n          # Randomly select a circle to perturb\n          idx_to_perturb = np.random.randint(0, n_circles)\n          \n          # Apply a small random perturbation to the selected center\n          current_centers[idx_to_perturb] += np.random.uniform(-perturbation_strength, perturbation_strength, 2)\n          current_centers[idx_to_perturb] = np.clip(current_centers[idx_to_perturb], 0.0, 1.0)\n          \n          # Compute radii and score for the new configuration\n          current_radii = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n          current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n\
    \          \n          # If the new configuration is better, accept it\n          if current_score > best_score_run:\n              best_score_run = current_score\n              best_centers_run = current_centers\n              # print(f\"  Step {step+1}/{num_steps}: New best score: {best_score_run:.6f}\") # Too verbose\n      \n      return best_score_run, best_centers_run, best_radii_run\n\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 26 circles in the unit square using a multiple restarts local search.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n              - centers: np.ndarray of shape (26, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n              - radii: np.ndarray of shape (26,) with radius of each circle\n      \"\"\"\n      n_circles = 26\n      \n      # Define the baseline initial configuration for centers\n      baseline_centers = np.zeros((n_circles, 2))\n      baseline_centers[0] = [0.5, 0.5]\n      \n      for i\
    \ in range(8):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / 8\n          baseline_centers[i + 1] = [0.5 + 0.25 * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + 0.25 * np.sin(angle)]\n      \n      for i in range(16):\n          angle = 2 * np.pi * i / 16\n          baseline_centers[i + 9] = [0.5 + 0.4 * np.cos(angle), 0.5 + 0.4 * np.sin(angle)]\n      \n      baseline_centers[25] = [0.5, 0.7]\n      baseline_centers = np.clip(baseline_centers, 0.05, 0.95) # Apply initial clipping\n\n      # Multiple Restarts parameters\n      num_restarts = 5\n      num_perturbation_steps = 5000\n      perturbation_strength = 0.018\n      random_initial_offset_scale = 0.005 # Small random offset for each restart\n\n      overall_best_score = -np.inf\n      overall_best_centers = None\n      overall_best_radii = None\n\n      print(f\"Starting {num_restarts} local search runs...\")\n\n      for run_idx in range(num_restarts):\n          print(f\"--- Running Local Search Restart {run_idx + 1}/{num_restarts} ---\")\n          run_score, run_centers,\
    \ run_radii = run_local_search(\n              baseline_centers,\n              num_perturbation_steps,\n              perturbation_strength,\n              random_initial_offset_scale\n          )\n          print(f\"  Run {run_idx + 1} finished with score: {run_score:.6f}\")\n\n          if run_score > overall_best_score:\n              overall_best_score = run_score\n              overall_best_centers = np.copy(run_centers)\n              overall_best_radii = np.copy(run_radii)\n              print(f\"  New overall best score: {overall_best_score:.6f}\")\n      \n      print(f\"Final overall best score after {num_restarts} restarts: {overall_best_score:.6f}\")\n      \n      if overall_best_centers is None: # Fallback if no valid solution found (shouldn't happen)\n          overall_best_centers = baseline_centers\n          overall_best_radii = compute_max_radii(baseline_centers)\n\n      return overall_best_centers, overall_best_radii\n```"
