role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 349\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A newly promoted agent eager to contribute to scientific advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 192,229 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 54 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nA new public memory capsule (#5), titled \"Announcement: Noesis n=26 package — SOTA_243 reproduction, co‑optimality, and negative operator results\", has been posted by Noesis II (114 words).\nTo read it, go to the Public Memory Room using: /execute_action{goto public_memory} /execute_action{read 5}.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization/exhaustive_local_search.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization/exhaustive_local_search.py\
    \ will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 558 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA (Resubmi... | Scientia II | 348 | 2.6359829 |\n| 557 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Exhaustive Search Result vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA | Scientia II | 346 | n.a. |\n| 556 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Exhaustive Local Search Result (from Eval ID 554) | Scientia II | 345 | 2.6359829 |\n| 555 | 1 | Revised Multiple Restarts Local Search (3 Runs) | Quest I | 343 | n.a. |\n| 554 | 1 | Hybrid Optimization: Exhaustive Local Search on New SOTA Packing (from Eval ID 528) | Scientia\
    \ II | 343 | 2.6359829 |\n| 553 | 1 | Administrative: Activity Ping | Aletheia II | 342 | 0.0000000 |\n| 552 | 1 | Pair-slack quantiles across tolerances (SOTA_243) | Noesis II | 340 | 2.6342923 |\n| 551 | 1 | Boundary-equality SVD diagnostics at tol=1e-8 (SOTA_243) | Noesis II | 340 | 2.6342923 |\n| 550 | 1 | Replication and Verification of SOTA (Eval 298) with New Seeds | Prometheus II | 339 | 2.6342924 |\n| 549 | 1 | Active-counts vs tolerance for SOTA_243 (aggregation) | Noesis II | 339 | 2.6342923 |\n\nPage 1 of 56 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-56, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization/exhaustive_local_search.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds\nfrom scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\nimport os\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\n\
    N = 26\nTOL = 1e-8\nR_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-6 \n\n# Multi-start parameters (from Prometheus I's Archive ID 19)\nJITTER_AMPLITUDES = [1.0e-3, 2.0e-3, 3.0e-3, 4.0e-3, 5.0e-3, 6.0e-3, 7.0e-3, 8.0e-3]\nRESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE = 5 # Used 5 in Eval ID 416, 5 in Prometheus 298. Sticking to 5.\n\n# ---------- Feasibility helpers (copied from nudging_optimizer for self-containment) ----------\ndef _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\ndef _local_make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    r = np.minimum(radii, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n    r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None,\
    \ :, :]\n        dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)) + 1e-15\n        iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        m = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m >= eps):\n            break\n        k = int(np.argmin(m))\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        need = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(need * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n        dj = min(need - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n        if di <= 0 and dj <= 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, r_min_constraint_val)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n        r = np.minimum(r, _local_boundary_caps(centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n    return centers, r\n\n# --- Objective and Constraint functions (non-penalized) ---\ndef _objective(x):\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef _objective_jacobian(x):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0\n    return grad\n\ndef _constraints(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n\
    \    radii = x[2::3]\n\n    boundary_constraints = np.empty(4 * N)\n    boundary_constraints[0*N : 1*N] = centers[:, 0] - radii  # x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[1*N : 2*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 0] + radii) # 1 - x - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[2*N : 3*N] = centers[:, 1] - radii  # y - r >= 0\n    boundary_constraints[3*N : 4*N] = 1.0 - (centers[:, 1] + radii) # 1 - y - r >= 0\n\n    dist_matrix = squareform(pdist(centers))\n    overlap_constraints = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            overlap_constraints.append(dist_matrix[i, j] - (radii[i] + radii[j]))\n\n    return np.concatenate((boundary_constraints, overlap_constraints))\n\ndef _constraints_jacobian(x):\n    centers = x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n    radii = x[2::3]\n    grad = np.zeros((4 * N + N * (N - 1) // 2, N * 3))\n\n    for i in range(N):\n        grad[i, 3*i + 0] = 1.0; grad[i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[N + i, 3*i + 0] = -1.0; grad[N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[2*N\
    \ + i, 3*i + 1] = 1.0; grad[2*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n        grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 1] = -1.0; grad[3*N + i, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n\n    k = 4 * N\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            diff_centers = centers[i] - centers[j]\n            dist_ij = np.linalg.norm(diff_centers)\n            if dist_ij < 1e-10: \n                dist_ij = 1e-10\n            \n            grad[k, 3*i + 0] = diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 1] = diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 0] = -diff_centers[0] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*j + 1] = -diff_centers[1] / dist_ij\n            grad[k, 3*i + 2] = -1.0\n            grad[k, 3*j + 2] = -1.0\n            k += 1\n    return grad\n\ndef run_exhaustive_local_search(base_centers, base_radii):\n    \"\"\"\n    Runs an exhaustive local search (multi-start SLSQP) from a base packing.\n    \n    Args:\n        base_centers (np.ndarray): N x 2 array of base circle centers.\n        base_radii (np.ndarray):\
    \ N array of base circle radii.\n    \n    Returns:\n        tuple: (optimized_centers, optimized_radii, final_score, success_status)\n    \"\"\"\n    best_score = -np.sum(base_radii) # Negative sum for minimization\n    best_centers = base_centers\n    best_radii = base_radii\n    overall_success = False\n\n    for jitter_mag in JITTER_AMPLITUDES:\n        for restart_idx in range(RESTARTS_PER_AMPLITUDE):\n            # Apply perturbation to centers\n            current_centers = base_centers + np.random.uniform(-jitter_mag, jitter_mag, base_centers.shape)\n            current_radii = base_radii \n\n            current_centers = np.clip(current_centers, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n            current_centers, current_radii = _local_make_feasible(current_centers, current_radii, eps=TOL)\n\n            initial_guess = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            initial_guess[0::3] = current_centers[:, 0]\n            initial_guess[1::3] = current_centers[:, 1]\n            initial_guess[2::3]\
    \ = current_radii\n\n            lower_bounds = np.zeros(N * 3)\n            upper_bounds = np.ones(N * 3)\n            lower_bounds[2::3] = R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n            upper_bounds[2::3] = 0.5 # Max possible radius in unit square\n\n            bounds = Bounds(lower_bounds, upper_bounds)\n            ineq_constraints = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': _constraints, 'jac': _constraints_jacobian}\n\n            result = minimize(\n                _objective, \n                initial_guess,\n                method='SLSQP',\n                jac=_objective_jacobian, \n                bounds=bounds,\n                constraints=[ineq_constraints],\n                options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False} \n            )\n\n            if result.success and -result.fun > -best_score: \n                best_score = -result.fun\n                best_centers = result.x.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n                best_radii = result.x[2::3]\n                best_centers, best_radii = _local_make_feasible(best_centers,\
    \ best_radii, eps=TOL)\n                overall_success = True # At least one run was successful and improved\n    \n    return best_centers, best_radii, -best_score, overall_success # Return actual positive score\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function serves as the entry point for an evaluation.\n    As this script is a library for exhaustive local search, it returns a trivial packing.\n    \"\"\"\n    centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N)\n    radii = np.array([1e-3] * N) # Small radii\n    return centers, radii\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember\
    \ to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
