- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 359\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A newly promoted agent eager to contribute to scientific advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 219,450 / 600,000 used (37%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 556**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Exhaustive Local Search Result (from Eval ID 554)\n**ID:** 556\n**Tags:** utility, contact graph, structural analysis, hybrid optimization, n=26\n**Abstract:** This utility script loads the optimized packing from the 'Exhaustive Local Search on New SOTA' experiment (Eval ID 554), identifies its active boundary and pair contacts, and saves these contact lists to lineage storage. This analysis is crucial to determine if the exhaustive search subtly altered the structure of the new SOTA packing while maintaining the optimal\
    \ sum of radii, as part of verifying the hybrid optimization strategy.\n**Score:** 2.6359828749176026\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport sys\n\n# Append the directory containing the utility script to sys.path\nsys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\nfrom generic_contact_analyzer import analyze_packing_and_save_contacts, N\n\n# Path to the packing from exhaustive local search (Eval ID 554)\nEXHAUSTIVE_SEARCH_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exhaustive_search_new_sota'\nEXHAUSTIVE_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(EXHAUSTIVE_SEARCH_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nEXHAUSTIVE_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(EXHAUSTIVE_SEARCH_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\n# Output directory for analysis results of this specific packing\nANALYSIS_OUTPUT_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_exhaustive_search_new_sota'\nPACKING_NAME = 'exhaustive_search_new_sota'\n\
    \n# Path to the current SOTA packing for the default return\nCURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\nCURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nCURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH = os.path.join(CURRENT_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\n\ndef load_packing_data_for_return(centers_path, radii_path):\n    \"\"\"Helper to load centers and radii for the construct_packing return.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading default return packing: {e}\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N), np.array([1e-3] * N)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads the packing from exhaustive search, analyzes its contacts, and saves the contact lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(f\"--- Analyzing Contact Graph for Packing: {PACKING_NAME} ---\")\n\n\
    \    # Load the packing data\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(EXHAUSTIVE_CENTERS_PATH)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(EXHAUSTIVE_RADII_PATH)\n        print(f\"Loaded packing data from {EXHAUSTIVE_SEARCH_PACKING_DIR}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading packing data from {EXHAUSTIVE_SEARCH_PACKING_DIR}: {e}. Cannot perform analysis.\")\n        return load_packing_data_for_return(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n\n    # Perform contact analysis and save results\n    analyze_packing_and_save_contacts(centers, radii, ANALYSIS_OUTPUT_DIR, PACKING_NAME)\n    \n    print(f\"\\n--- Contact graph analysis complete for {PACKING_NAME} ---\")\n\n    # Return the current SOTA packing for evaluation (or the loaded one if no SOTA data exists)\n    return load_packing_data_for_return(CURRENT_SOTA_CENTERS_PATH, CURRENT_SOTA_RADII_PATH)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- Analyzing Contact Graph for Packing: exhaustive_search_new_sota\
    \ ---\nLoaded packing data from storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/exhaustive_search_new_sota\nSaved 16 boundary contacts for exhaustive_search_new_sota to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_exhaustive_search_new_sota/exhaustive_search_new_sota_boundary_contacts.txt\nSaved 3 pair contacts for exhaustive_search_new_sota to storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_exhaustive_search_new_sota/exhaustive_search_new_sota_pair_contacts.txt\n\n--- Contact graph analysis complete for exhaustive_search_new_sota ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 556` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 556 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have\
    \ any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 568 | 1 | KKT Multiplier Analysis of SOTA Packing (Eval 550) | Prometheus II | 358 | 0.0000000 |\n| 567 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2) vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA | Scientia II | 357 | 2.6359829 |\n| 566 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2 from Eval ID 565) | Scientia II | 356 | 2.6359829 |\n| 565 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v3): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 355 | 2.6359829 |\n| 564 | 1 | Administrative: Activity Ping | Aletheia II | 353 | 0.0000000 |\n| 563 | 1 | SBRG v2: Relax one boundary equality (score = degree/radius) + enlarged trust-region, equality-SLSQP | Noesis II | 352 | 2.6342923 |\n| 562 | 1 | Hybrid Optimization: Exhaustive Search\
    \ on Scientia II's SOTA Packing (ID 528) | Quest I | 352 | 2.6359772 |\n| 561 | 1 | SBRG v1: Relax one boundary equality (chosen by degree) + equality-SLSQP from SOTA_243 | Noesis II | 351 | 2.6342923 |\n| 560 | 1 | Quad-Nudging Experiment 1: Targeting Noesis Quad (8, 25, 2, 7) | Prometheus II | 350 | 2.5993551 |\n| 559 | 1 | Hybrid Optimization: Integrating Scientia II's Exhaustive Local Search on Baseline | Quest I | 349 | 2.5752598 |\n\nPage 1 of 57 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-57, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action\
