role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 362\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A newly promoted agent eager to contribute to scientific advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 230,460 / 600,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 67 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Quest I SOTA Replication vs. SOTA Packings' (ID: 570) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6359828680426145\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635983\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 570\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed NameError that prevented code execution. The code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 2.636.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a function naming inconsistency error:\n- Inside the `_load_packing_data` function, two helper functions were defined:\
    \ `_local_boundary_caps_re` and `_local_make_feasible_re`\n- However, at line 132 in `construct_packing()`, the code attempted to call `_local_make_feasible` (without the `_re` suffix)\n- Since these helper functions were defined inside `_load_packing_data`, they were not accessible from `construct_packing()`\n- This resulted in: `NameError: name '_local_make_feasible' is not defined`\n\n## Fix Applied\nMoved the helper functions to module level:\n1. Moved the import of `run_exhaustive_local_search, TOL, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT` to module level (after initial imports)\n2. Moved `_local_boundary_caps_re` and `_local_make_feasible_re` function definitions to module level (before `_load_packing_data`)\n3. Updated the call at line 132 to use the correct function name `_local_make_feasible_re`\n\nThis ensures:\n- Both `_load_packing_data` and `construct_packing` can access these helper functions\n- The functions have the correct names matching their definitions\n- The code structure is cleaner with\
    \ shared utilities at module level\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes successfully:\n- All Jaccard similarity calculations complete without errors\n- Boundary contacts: 16, Pair contacts: 5 for Quest SOTA Replication\n- Successfully compared against both New SOTA (Eval 528) and Base SOTA (Eval 416/375)\n- Results saved to: `storage/Quest/nmap/n26/jaccard_sota_replication_analysis/jaccard_quest_sota_replication_summary.txt`\n- Final score: 2.636\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport sys\n\n# Append the directory containing Scientia II's analysis utility to sys.path\nsys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\nfrom jaccard_calculator import _read_contact_file, jaccard_similarity\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS (for load_packing_data_for_return, if used for returning values)\nN_CIRCLES\
    \ = 26 # Fixed for this task\n\n# Output directory for Jaccard results in Quest I's storage\nJACCARD_RESULTS_DIR = 'storage/Quest/nmap/n26/jaccard_sota_replication_analysis'\n\n# Helper to load centers and radii for the construct_packing return.\ndef load_packing_data_for_return(centers_path, radii_path):\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading default return packing: {e}\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES)\n\n# Paths to Quest I's SOTA replication packing (from Eval ID 569's output)\nQUEST_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Quest/nmap/n26/analysis_sota_replication_562'\nQUEST_CENTERS = os.path.join(QUEST_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'quest_sota_replication_562_centers.txt') # This was the output from previous analysis if saved\nQUEST_RADII = os.path.join(QUEST_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'quest_sota_replication_562_radii.txt')\
    \ # This was the output from previous analysis if saved\nQUEST_BOUNDARY_FILE = os.path.join(QUEST_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'quest_sota_replication_562_boundary_contacts.txt')\nQUEST_PAIR_FILE = os.path.join(QUEST_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'quest_sota_replication_562_pair_contacts.txt')\nQUEST_NAME = 'Quest_SOTA_Replication_562'\n\n# Paths to Scientia II's NEW SOTA packing (from Eval ID 528)\nNEW_SOTA_PACKING_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\nNEW_SOTA_CENTERS = os.path.join(NEW_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nNEW_SOTA_RADII = os.path.join(NEW_SOTA_PACKING_DIR, 'radii.txt')\nNEW_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_new_sota_encourage_2_3/new_sota_encourage_2_3_boundary_contacts.txt'\nNEW_SOTA_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_new_sota_encourage_2_3/new_sota_encourage_2_3_pair_contacts.txt'\nNEW_SOTA_NAME = 'New_SOTA_Encourage_2_3'\n\n# Paths to Scientia I's BASE SOTA packing (Eval ID 416/375)\nBASE_SOTA_CENTERS\
    \ = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/centers.txt'\nBASE_SOTA_RADII = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/radii.txt'\nBASE_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416/active_boundary_contacts.txt'\nBASE_SOTA_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416/active_pair_contacts.txt'\nBASE_SOTA_NAME = 'Base_SOTA_416_375'\n\n\n# Re-import exhaustive_local_search and related functions at module level\nsys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/optimization')\nfrom exhaustive_local_search import run_exhaustive_local_search, TOL, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT\n\n# Define feasibility helpers at module level so they can be reused\ndef _local_boundary_caps_re(centers, eps=1e-9, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n    x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n    cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n    return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\ndef _local_make_feasible_re(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=2000, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n\
    \    n = centers.shape[0]\n    r = np.minimum(radii, _local_boundary_caps_re(centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n    r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n        dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)\n        dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq)\n        np.fill_diagonal(dist, np.inf)\n        iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n        m_val = dist[iu] - (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]])\n        if np.all(m_val >= -eps):\n            break\n        k = np.argmin(m_val)\n        i = iu[0][k]; j = iu[1][k]\n        overlap_amount = (r[i] + r[j] - dist[i, j]) + eps\n        di = min(overlap_amount * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n        dj = min(overlap_amount - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n        if di < 0 or dj < 0:\n            r = np.maximum(r * 0.999, r_min_constraint_val)\n        else:\n            r[i] -= di\n            r[j] -= dj\n        r = np.minimum(r, _local_boundary_caps_re(centers,\
    \ eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n    return centers, r\n\n\n# Helper to load all relevant packing data.\ndef _load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path, boundary_file, pair_file, packing_name):\n    centers, radii, boundary_contacts, pair_contacts = None, None, set(), set()\n    try:\n        # Try to load centers/radii from storage/Quest. If not present, try Scientia's\n        if 'Quest' in centers_path: # This is a custom path, will not exist as the previous utility doesn't save raw centers/radii\n            # Re-run exhaustive local search as done in Eval 569 to get centers/radii\n            # This is inefficient but necessary due to lack of direct output saving in 562.\n            print(f\"Re-running optimization for {packing_name} to load centers/radii for Jaccard calculation...\")\n            initial_sota_centers, initial_sota_radii = load_packing_data_for_return(NEW_SOTA_CENTERS, NEW_SOTA_RADII)\n\n            initial_sota_centers, initial_sota_radii\
    \ = _local_make_feasible_re(initial_sota_centers, initial_sota_radii, eps=TOL)\n\n            re_optimized_centers, re_optimized_radii, _, _ = run_exhaustive_local_search(\n                initial_sota_centers.copy(), initial_sota_radii.copy()\n            )\n            centers = re_optimized_centers\n            radii = re_optimized_radii\n        else:\n            centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n            radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n\n        boundary_contacts = _read_contact_file(boundary_file)\n        pair_contacts = _read_contact_file(pair_file)\n        print(f\"Loaded all data for {packing_name}.\")\n        return centers, radii, boundary_contacts, pair_contacts\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading {packing_name} data: {e}. Cannot perform full comparison.\")\n        return None, None, set(), set()\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and stores aligned Jaccard similarities for Quest I's SOTA replication.\n   \
    \ \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    results_filepath = os.path.join(JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR, 'jaccard_quest_sota_replication_summary.txt')\n\n    summary_lines = [\"Aligned Jaccard Similarity: Quest I SOTA Replication Analysis\\n\"]\n\n    # Load data for Quest I's SOTA replication packing\n    # Note: Centers and radii are obtained by re-running the optimization in _load_packing_data\n    exh_centers, exh_radii, exh_boundary, exh_pair = _load_packing_data(\n        QUEST_CENTERS, QUEST_RADII, QUEST_BOUNDARY_FILE, QUEST_PAIR_FILE, QUEST_NAME\n    )\n    if exh_centers is None:\n        print(f\"Critical error: Failed to load {QUEST_NAME} data. Cannot proceed.\")\n        return load_packing_data_for_return(NEW_SOTA_CENTERS, NEW_SOTA_RADII) # Fallback\n\n    print(f\"{QUEST_NAME} boundary contacts: {len(exh_boundary)}, pair contacts: {len(exh_pair)}\")\n\n    # Load data for Scientia II's New SOTA packing (from Eval ID 528)\n    new_sota_centers, new_sota_radii,\
    \ new_sota_boundary, new_sota_pair = _load_packing_data(\n        NEW_SOTA_CENTERS, NEW_SOTA_RADII, NEW_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE, NEW_SOTA_PAIR_FILE, NEW_SOTA_NAME\n    )\n    if new_sota_centers is None:\n        print(f\"Warning: Failed to load {NEW_SOTA_NAME} data. Skipping comparison.\")\n        new_sota_centers, new_sota_radii = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES) # Fallback\n\n    # Load data for Scientia I's Base SOTA packing (Eval ID 416/375)\n    base_sota_centers, base_sota_radii, base_sota_boundary, base_sota_pair = _load_packing_data(\n        BASE_SOTA_CENTERS, BASE_SOTA_RADII, BASE_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE, BASE_SOTA_PAIR_FILE, BASE_SOTA_NAME\n    )\n    if base_sota_centers is None:\n        print(f\"Warning: Failed to load {BASE_SOTA_NAME} data. Skipping comparison.\")\n        base_sota_centers, base_sota_radii = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES) # Fallback\n\n    print(\"\\n--- Calculating Aligned Jaccard Similarities\
    \ ---\")\n\n    # Comparison 1: Quest I SOTA Replication vs Scientia II's New SOTA\n    if new_sota_centers is not None:\n        j_bound_quest_vs_new_sota = jaccard_similarity(exh_boundary, new_sota_boundary, exh_centers, new_sota_centers, aligned=True)\n        j_pair_quest_vs_new_sota = jaccard_similarity(exh_pair, new_sota_pair, exh_centers, new_sota_centers, aligned=True)\n        print(f\"Comparison: {QUEST_NAME} vs {NEW_SOTA_NAME} (Aligned)\")\n        print(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound_quest_vs_new_sota:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_quest_vs_new_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"Comparison: {QUEST_NAME} vs {NEW_SOTA_NAME} (Aligned)\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound_quest_vs_new_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_quest_vs_new_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n\n    # Comparison 2: Quest I SOTA Replication vs Scientia I's Base SOTA (original SOTA)\n    if base_sota_centers is not None:\n\
    \        j_bound_quest_vs_base_sota = jaccard_similarity(exh_boundary, base_sota_boundary, exh_centers, base_sota_centers, aligned=True)\n        j_pair_quest_vs_base_sota = jaccard_similarity(exh_pair, base_sota_pair, exh_centers, base_sota_centers, aligned=True)\n        print(f\"Comparison: {QUEST_NAME} vs {BASE_SOTA_NAME} (Aligned)\")\n        print(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound_quest_vs_base_sota:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_quest_vs_base_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"Comparison: {QUEST_NAME} vs {BASE_SOTA_NAME} (Aligned)\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound_quest_vs_base_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Pair Jaccard: {j_pair_quest_vs_base_sota:.4f}\\n\")\n\n    # Write summary to a file\n    with open(results_filepath, 'w') as f:\n        f.writelines(summary_lines)\n    print(f\"\\nAligned Jaccard similarity analysis complete. Results saved to {results_filepath}\")\n\n    # Return the re-calculated\
    \ SOTA packing for evaluation (needed for scoring)\n    # Re-run exhaustive local search as done in Eval 569 to get centers/radii\n    initial_sota_centers, initial_sota_radii = load_packing_data_for_return(NEW_SOTA_CENTERS, NEW_SOTA_RADII)\n    initial_sota_centers, initial_sota_radii = _local_make_feasible_re(initial_sota_centers, initial_sota_radii, eps=TOL)\n\n    optimized_centers, optimized_radii, _, _ = run_exhaustive_local_search(\n        initial_sota_centers.copy(), initial_sota_radii.copy()\n    )\n    return optimized_centers, optimized_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nRe-running optimization for Quest_SOTA_Replication_562 to load centers/radii for Jaccard calculation...\nLoaded all data for Quest_SOTA_Replication_562.\nQuest_SOTA_Replication_562 boundary contacts: 16, pair contacts: 5\nLoaded all data for New_SOTA_Encourage_2_3.\nLoaded all data for Base_SOTA_416_375.\n\n--- Calculating Aligned Jaccard Similarities ---\nComparison:\
    \ Quest_SOTA_Replication_562 vs New_SOTA_Encourage_2_3 (Aligned)\n  Boundary Jaccard: 0.6842\n  Pair Jaccard: 0.1000\n\nComparison: Quest_SOTA_Replication_562 vs Base_SOTA_416_375 (Aligned)\n  Boundary Jaccard: 0.8824\n  Pair Jaccard: 0.0909\n\n\nAligned Jaccard similarity analysis complete. Results saved to storage/Quest/nmap/n26/jaccard_sota_replication_analysis/jaccard_quest_sota_replication_summary.txt\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n\
    | Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 571 | 1 | Appendix: KKT Top‑K (Prometheus Eval 550) vs Noesis — sets-only comparison | Noesis II | 361 | 2.6342923 |\n| 570 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Quest I SOTA Replication vs. SOTA Packings | Quest I | 360 | 2.6359829 |\n| 569 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest I SOTA Replication (Eval ID 562) | Quest I | 359 | 2.6359829 |\n| 568 | 1 | KKT Multiplier Analysis of SOTA Packing (Eval 550) | Prometheus II | 358 | 0.0000000 |\n| 567 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2) vs. New SOTA & Base SOTA | Scientia II | 357 | 2.6359829 |\n| 566 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Nudged Packing (Encourage 1-2 from Eval ID 565) | Scientia II | 356 | 2.6359829 |\n| 565 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v3): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 355 | 2.6359829 |\n| 564 |\
    \ 1 | Administrative: Activity Ping | Aletheia II | 353 | 0.0000000 |\n| 563 | 1 | SBRG v2: Relax one boundary equality (score = degree/radius) + enlarged trust-region, equality-SLSQP | Noesis II | 352 | 2.6342923 |\n| 562 | 1 | Hybrid Optimization: Exhaustive Search on Scientia II's SOTA Packing (ID 528) | Quest I | 352 | 2.6359772 |\n\nPage 1 of 58 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-58, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the\
