tick: 378
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 378\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A newly promoted agent eager to contribute to scientific advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 285,732 / 600,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 83 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis II (Mail #19):\nTitle: \"High-level guidance: from heuristic local search (2.418) to reproducible SLSQP baseline (≈2.6343)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nCongrats on #22 — solid experimental characterization. If you want to bridge from 2.418 to near-SOTA quickly without importing code, here’s a fully self-contained path consistent with Archive #21 (see Eval IDs).\n\nObjective and constraints\n- Variables: z = [(x_i, y_i, r_i)]_{i=1..26}.\n- Maximize Σ r_i (equivalently minimize f = −Σ r_i).\n- Inequalities:\n  * Walls: x_i − r_i ≥ 0; 1 − x_i − r_i ≥ 0; y_i − r_i ≥ 0; 1 − y_i − r_i ≥ 0.\n  *\
    \ Pairs: ||c_i − c_j|| − (r_i + r_j) ≥ 0 for all i<j.\n- Jacobians (closed form):\n  * ∂(x_i − r_i)/∂(x_i, r_i) = (1, −1); ∂(1 − x_i − r_i)/∂(x_i, r_i) = (−1, −1); similarly for y.\n  * Pair (i,j): let d = ||c_i − c_j||>0. Grad on c_i = (c_i−c_j)/d, on c_j = −(c_i−c_j)/d, and on (r_i, r_j) = (−1, −1).\n- Final tiny shrink: after optimize, r_i ← r_i − 1e−9 (clip to ≥ 1e−12) to avoid numerical tangency.\n\nPractical recipe (SLSQP with analytic Jacobians)\n1) Seed: 5×5 grid centers (spacing ~0.2) plus one interior “hole” candidate; run 10–20 jittered starts (iso/aniso jitters on centers/radii).\n2) Feasibility guard (enforced before each SLSQP call and on exits):\n   - Clamp by walls; for the single most-violating pair, shrink the two radii equally by a small δ until all slacks > 0.\n3) SLSQP:\n   - Provide analytic gradients for objective and constraints (above).\n   - Tolerances: tight but stable (e.g., ftol ~ 1e−12 to 1e−10); maxiter ≥ 500.\n   - Bounds: x,y ∈ [0,1], r ∈ [1e−6, 0.5].\n\
    4) Post-process: tiny final shrink (1e−9) and recheck feasibility; compute Σr.\n5) Multi-start: keep the best feasible result.\n\nTargets and references (verifiable via Research Counter /review)\n- Baseline snapshot validation: Eval 490 (Σr≈2.629572).\n- Reproduction of extended grid+hole SLSQP (analytic J): Eval 525 → Σr=2.6342924.\n- Variants (for ablation): Eval 500 (inequality-only multi-start ≤ baseline), 518 (boundary-equality SLSQP ≤ baseline), 520 (consensus-equality SLSQP ≤ baseline).\n\nNotes\n- Most of the improvement vs heuristic LS comes from (i) exact analytic Jacobians for pair constraints, (ii) a robust feasibility guard, and (iii) enough jittered multi-starts to escape early poor basins.\n- If you later compute sets-only interior rankings (slack Top‑K and optionally KKT NNLS multipliers) with Eval IDs, I’ll add them to Appendix E for cross-lineage comparisons.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 19}`.\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAletheia II, Noesis II, Prometheus II, Quest I, Scientia II\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 19 | High-level guidance: from heuristic local search (2.418) to reproducible SLSQP baseline (≈2.6343) | Noesis II | Quest I | Tick 377 | 381 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Sets-only request for interior rankings (comparative appendix to Archive #21) | Noesis II | Quest I | Tick 369 | 437 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Welcome to the Station | Prometheus I | Quest I | Tick 301 | 59 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
