    \ restart from feasible sum of radii: 0.000000\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.627798\n--- Restart 3/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03) ---\n  Starting SLSQP for this restart from feasible sum of radii: 0.000000\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.621974\n--- Restart 4/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03) ---\n  Starting SLSQP for this restart from feasible sum of radii: 0.000000\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.627207\n--- Restart 5/5 (Jitter: 5.000e-03) ---\n  Starting SLSQP for this restart from feasible sum of radii: 0.000000\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.628410\n  New overall best score: 2.628410\nFinal best score after 10 multi-start SLSQP runs: 2.628410\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious\
    \ red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Self-Contained Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization with Jittered 5x5 Grid Seeds' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 602.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 603 | 1 | Utility: Scientia boundary v2 — schema-aligned parse (boundary_equalities,\
    \ disc/side @ tol=1e-8) | Noesis II | 387 | 2.6342923 |\n| 602 | 1 | Self-Contained Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization with Jittered 5x5 Grid Seeds | Quest I | 387 | 2.6284096 |\n| 601 | 1 | Nudging Experiment (v5): Automated Target Identification by Encouraging Further Selected Near-Con... | Scientia II | 386 | 2.6359829 |\n| 600 | 1 | SLSQP Debugging Attempt 2: Proactive Center Separation & Robust Jacobian | Quest I | 385 | 2.6191058 |\n| 599 | 1 | Simulated Annealing v3: JAX/GPU Implementation for Performance | Prometheus II | 384 | n.a. |\n| 598 | 1 | Utility: Sets-only comparison vs Scientia SOTA 528 — boundary and Top-K slack (1e-9/1e-8) | Noesis II | 384 | 2.6342923 |\n| 597 | 1 | SLSQP Debugging Attempt 1: Robust Feasibility & R_MIN_CONSTRAINT Refinement | Quest I | 383 | 0.0000000 |\n| 596 | 1 | Utility: Export Scientia II SOTA Contact Data for Noesis II Comparative Appendix | Scientia II | 383 | 2.6359829 |\n| 595 | 1 | Utility: Boundary Jaccard tol-grid vs Quest Eval 562 (1e-8,\
    \ 2e-8, 5e-8) | Noesis II | 382 | 2.6342923 |\n| 594 | 1 | Self-Contained SLSQP Optimization with Analytic Gradients on 5x5 Grid Seed | Quest I | 381 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 61 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-61, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
