parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 415\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A newly promoted agent eager to contribute to scientific advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 453,251 / 600,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 120 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SLSQP Multi-Start Tuning: Robust Feasibility with Targeted Center Perturbation' (ID: 657) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.630956600495699\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.630957\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Multi-Start SLSQP optimization with 24 restarts (6 amplitudes x 4 restarts/amplitude).\n--- Restart 1/4 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart:\
    \ 0.240046\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.620520\n  New overall best score: 2.620520\n--- Restart 2/4 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.240053\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.624510\n  New overall best score: 2.624510\n--- Restart 3/4 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.240079\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.619106\n--- Restart 4/4 (Jitter: 1.000e-04) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.240092\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.624510\n--- Restart 1/4 (Jitter: 1.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.241295\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.628070\n  New overall best score: 2.628070\n--- Restart 2/4 (Jitter: 1.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.242189\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.628070\n--- Restart 3/4 (Jitter: 1.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.240312\n  Restart failed: Inequality constraints incompatible\n\
    --- Restart 4/4 (Jitter: 1.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.241081\n  Restart failed: Positive directional derivative for linesearch\n--- Restart 1/4 (Jitter: 3.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.241161\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.625767\n--- Restart 2/4 (Jitter: 3.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.242025\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.620159\n--- Restart 3/4 (Jitter: 3.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.242423\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.599553\n--- Restart 4/4 (Jitter: 3.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.245335\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.630957\n  New overall best score: 2.630957\n--- Restart 1/4 (Jitter: 6.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.250360\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.628570\n--- Restart 2/4 (Jitter: 6.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.251830\n  Restart successful.\
    \ Final score: 2.628522\n--- Restart 3/4 (Jitter: 6.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.249628\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.630957\n  New overall best score: 2.630957\n--- Restart 4/4 (Jitter: 6.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.242479\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.621727\n--- Restart 1/4 (Jitter: 9.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.243123\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.618187\n--- Restart 2/4 (Jitter: 9.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.247560\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.621667\n--- Restart 3/4 (Jitter: 9.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.243853\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.618809\n--- Restart 4/4 (Jitter: 9.000e-03) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.242076\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.612217\n--- Restart 1/4 (Jitter: 1.200e-02) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.256089\n  Restart\
    \ successful. Final score: 2.623786\n--- Restart 2/4 (Jitter: 1.200e-02) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.257458\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.621974\n--- Restart 3/4 (Jitter: 1.200e-02) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.247261\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.619679\n--- Restart 4/4 (Jitter: 1.200e-02) ---\n  Initial feasible score for this restart: 0.249420\n  Restart successful. Final score: 2.621974\nFinal best score after 24 multi-start SLSQP runs: 2.630957\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 453,251 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 600,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token\
    \ usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'SLSQP Multi-Start Tuning: Robust Feasibility with Targeted Center Perturbation' submitted\
    \ for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 657.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 657 | 1 | SLSQP Multi-Start Tuning: Robust Feasibility with Targeted Center Perturbation | Quest I | 414 | 2.6309566 |\n| 656 | 1 | Gate v1 Sensitivity Sweep on Noesis Snapshot: tol_grid × crossing(strict|inclusive) | Noesis II | 413 | 2.6342923 |\n| 655 | 1 | Exhaustive Search with Hexagonal Lattices | Axiom I | 412 | 2.6244306 |\n| 654 | 1 | Utility: Export Contact Data for Prometheus II SOTA (Eval 620) | Prometheus II | 412 | 0.0000000 |\n| 653 | 1 | SLSQP Multi-Start Tuning: Focused Jitter Amplitudes (5x6 Restarts) | Quest I | 412 | 2.6304384\
    \ |\n| 652 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2 (Bugfix): Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 411 | 2.6250545 |\n| 651 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP from Perturbed Hexagonal Lattices | Axiom I | 410 | 2.6244306 |\n| 650 | 1 | Hard Constraint Seeding 2: Locking Pair (6, 12) | Prometheus II | 410 | 0.0000000 |\n| 649 | 1 | SLSQP Multi-Start Tuning: Increased Restarts (6x5 Restarts) for Broader Exploration | Quest I | 410 | 2.6300860 |\n| 648 | 1 | Utility: Aligned Jaccard Comparison of Nudged Packing (Encourage 3-9) vs. Key SOTA Variants | Scientia II | 410 | 2.6359829 |\n\nPage 1 of 66 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-66, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
    \ (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
