tick: 419
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Quest I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have successfully pruned my private memory by deleting Capsule ID 3. This frees up tokens and optimizes my memory usage.\n\nNow, with a streamlined private memory and a clear strategy from my reflection, my next action is to implement the meticulously tuned Simulated Annealing (SA) algorithm. This directly addresses the limitations of my previous greedy local search and aims to break through the performance ceiling, as suggested by the reviewer of my published paper.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit this new SA experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Self-Contained Tuned Simulated Annealing on 5x5 Grid Seed\"\ntags: \"Simulated Annealing, metaheuristic, N=26, self-contained, optimization, local optima escape\"\nabstract: \"This submission presents a meticulously tuned, self-contained Simulated Annealing (SA) algorithm for the N=26 circle packing problem,\
    \ directly addressing the limitations of greedy local search identified in Archive ID 22. It utilizes a deterministic 5x5 grid + central circle seed, combined with a robust feasibility function. A principled annealing schedule is implemented (T_initial=1.0, T_final=1e-6 over 20,000 iterations, alpha=0.99931), along with differentiated perturbation strengths for centers (0.018) and radii (0.001). This aims to effectively escape local optima and achieve higher scores by intelligent exploration of the packing landscape.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, Bounds # Imported for consistency, not directly used in SA loop\n  from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist, squareform\n\n  # GLOBAL CONSTANTS (copied from my successful SLSQP implementations)\n  N = 26 # Number of circles\n  TOL = 1e-8 # General tolerance for feasibility checks\n  R_MIN_CONSTRAINT = 1e-12 # Minimum allowed radius for numerical stability\n\n  # --- SA Schedule and Perturbation Parameters\
    \ (from reflection) ---\n  T_INITIAL = 1.0\n  T_FINAL = 1e-6\n  NUM_ITERATIONS = 20000\n  ALPHA = (T_FINAL / T_INITIAL)**(1 / NUM_ITERATIONS) # Calculated cooling rate\n  CENTER_PERTURB_STRENGTH = 0.018\n  RADIUS_PERTURB_STRENGTH = 0.001\n\n  # --- Feasibility Helper Functions (copied from my robust SLSQP implementations, ID 642) ---\n  def _calculate_boundary_caps(centers, eps=1e-9, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT):\n      x = centers[:, 0]\n      y = centers[:, 1]\n      cap = np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y)) - eps\n      return np.maximum(cap, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n  def _make_feasible(centers, radii, eps=1e-9, max_iter=5000, r_min_constraint_val=R_MIN_CONSTRAINT): \n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      current_centers = np.copy(centers)\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              if np.allclose(current_centers[i], current_centers[j], atol=1e-12):\n                  perturb_amount = 1e-6 \n                  angle\
    \ = np.random.uniform(0, 2 * np.pi)\n                  current_centers[j] += np.array([perturb_amount * np.cos(angle), perturb_amount * np.sin(angle)])\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n      \n      r = np.minimum(radii, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n      r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n      for iteration in range(max_iter):\n          diff = current_centers[:, None, :] - current_centers[None, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=2)\n          dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) \n          \n          np.fill_diagonal(dist, np.inf) \n\n          iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1) \n          overlap_amounts = (r[iu[0]] + r[iu[1]]) - dist[iu] \n          \n          if np.all(overlap_amounts <= eps): \n              break\n          \n          k = np.argmax(overlap_amounts)\n          i = iu[0][k]\n          j = iu[1][k]\n      \
    \    \n          overlap_to_resolve = overlap_amounts[k] + eps \n\n          if overlap_to_resolve > 0.01: # Targeted Center Perturbation for severe overlaps\n              direction = current_centers[i] - current_centers[j]\n              norm_direction = np.linalg.norm(direction)\n              if norm_direction > 1e-10: \n                  unit_direction = direction / norm_direction\n                  move_amount = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.1, 0.005) \n                  \n                  current_centers[i] += unit_direction * move_amount\n                  current_centers[j] -= unit_direction * move_amount\n                  \n                  current_centers[i] = np.clip(current_centers[i], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n                  current_centers[j] = np.clip(current_centers[j], r_min_constraint_val, 1.0 - r_min_constraint_val)\n              \n              r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n\
    \              r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n\n          if dist[i,j] < 2 * r_min_constraint_val: \n              r[i] = r_min_constraint_val\n              r[j] = r_min_constraint_val\n          else:\n              di = min(overlap_to_resolve * 0.5, r[i] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              dj = min(overlap_to_resolve - di, r[j] - r_min_constraint_val)\n              r[i] -= di\n              r[j] -= dj\n          \n          r = np.minimum(r, _calculate_boundary_caps(current_centers, eps=eps, r_min_constraint_val=r_min_constraint_val))\n          r = np.maximum(r, r_min_constraint_val)\n          \n      return current_centers, r \n\n  # --- Helper functions for flat state representation ---\n  def _pack(centers, radii):\n      x_flat = np.zeros(N * 3)\n      x_flat[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n      x_flat[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n      x_flat[2::3] = radii\n      return x_flat\n\n  def _unpack(x_flat):\n      centers = x_flat.reshape(N, 3)[:, :2]\n      radii = x_flat[2::3]\n\
    \      return centers, radii\n\n  def _evaluate_score(centers, radii):\n      \"\"\"Calculates the sum of radii (score) for a given packing.\"\"\"\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Construct a packing of 26 circles in the unit square using a meticulously tuned\n      self-contained Simulated Annealing algorithm.\n      \n      Returns:\n          tuple: A tuple of (centers, radii) where:\n              - centers: np.ndarray of shape (26, 2) with (x, y) coordinates\n              - radii: np.ndarray of shape (26,) with radius of each circle\n      \"\"\"\n      # 1. Initialization - Deterministic 5x5 grid + central circle seed\n      initial_centers_base = []\n      grid_dim = 5\n      spacing = 1.0 / (grid_dim + 1)\n\n      for i in range(grid_dim):\n          for j in range(grid_dim):\n              x = (i + 1) * spacing\n              y = (j + 1) * spacing\n              initial_centers_base.append([x, y])\n      initial_centers_base.append([0.5,\
    \ 0.5]) \n      initial_centers_np = np.array(initial_centers_base)\n\n      # Initial guess for radii: A slightly larger, safe value\n      initial_radii_np = np.full(N, 0.01)\n\n      # Ensure initial state is strictly feasible using the robust _make_feasible\n      initial_centers, initial_radii = _make_feasible(initial_centers_np, initial_radii_np, eps=TOL)\n\n      # Pack initial state into flat vector\n      current_x_flat = _pack(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n      current_score = _evaluate_score(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n      current_energy = -current_score # Minimize negative score\n\n      best_x_flat = np.copy(current_x_flat)\n      best_score = current_score\n      best_energy = current_energy\n\n      temperature = T_INITIAL\n\n      print(f\"Starting Simulated Annealing. Initial feasible score: {current_score:.6f}\")\n      print(f\"Annealing Schedule: T_initial={T_INITIAL:.4f}, T_final={T_FINAL:.6f}, Num_iter={NUM_ITERATIONS}, Alpha={ALPHA:.5f}\")\n\n      #\
    \ SA loop\n      for step in range(NUM_ITERATIONS):\n          # Generate neighboring state\n          new_x_flat = np.copy(current_x_flat)\n          idx_to_perturb = np.random.randint(0, N) # Select one circle\n\n          # Perturb its x, y, and r\n          new_x_flat[3*idx_to_perturb + 0] += np.random.uniform(-CENTER_PERTURB_STRENGTH, CENTER_PERTURB_STRENGTH)\n          new_x_flat[3*idx_to_perturb + 1] += np.random.uniform(-CENTER_PERTURB_STRENGTH, CENTER_PERTURB_STRENGTH)\n          new_x_flat[3*idx_to_perturb + 2] += np.random.uniform(-RADIUS_PERTURB_STRENGTH, RADIUS_PERTURB_STRENGTH)\n          \n          # Unpack, clip to bounds, and make feasible\n          new_centers_raw, new_radii_raw = _unpack(new_x_flat)\n          new_centers_clipped = np.clip(new_centers_raw, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 1.0 - R_MIN_CONSTRAINT)\n          new_radii_clipped = np.clip(new_radii_raw, R_MIN_CONSTRAINT, 0.5)\n\n          feasible_new_centers, feasible_new_radii = _make_feasible(new_centers_clipped,\
    \ new_radii_clipped, eps=TOL)\n          \n          # Pack back to flat vector for current_x_flat management\n          new_x_flat_feasible = _pack(feasible_new_centers, feasible_new_radii)\n          new_score = _evaluate_score(feasible_new_centers, feasible_new_radii)\n          new_energy = -new_score\n\n          # Acceptance criterion (Metropolis-Hastings)\n          if new_energy < current_energy: # If new state is better, accept it\n              current_x_flat = np.copy(new_x_flat_feasible)\n              current_energy = new_energy\n              current_score = new_score\n          else: # If new state is worse, accept with a probability\n              if temperature > T_FINAL: # Only accept worse states if temperature is high enough\n                  acceptance_probability = np.exp(-(new_energy - current_energy) / temperature)\n                  if np.random.rand() < acceptance_probability:\n                      current_x_flat = np.copy(new_x_flat_feasible)\n          \
    \            current_energy = new_energy\n                      current_score = new_score\n          \n          # Update best score found so far globally\n          if current_score > best_score:\n              best_score = current_score\n              best_x_flat = np.copy(current_x_flat) # Store the flat vector\n              best_energy = current_energy\n              print(f\"Step {step+1}/{NUM_ITERATIONS}: New best score: {best_score:.6f} (T={temperature:.6f})\")\n              \n          # Cool down the system\n          temperature *= ALPHA\n\n          # Log progress every 1000 steps\n          if (step + 1) % 1000 == 0 or step == NUM_ITERATIONS - 1:\n              print(f\"Progress at Step {step+1}/{NUM_ITERATIONS}: Current Score={current_score:.6f}, Best Score={best_score:.6f}, T={temperature:.6f}\")\n\n      print(f\"Final best score after {NUM_ITERATIONS} SA steps: {best_score:.6f}\")\n\n      final_best_centers, final_best_radii = _unpack(best_x_flat)\n      return final_best_centers,\
    \ final_best_radii\n```"
