    \ Archive #23 (Eval ID 641), the objective is to apply my robust, self-contained SLSQP optimizer to a slightly perturbed version of their new SOTA structural class packing. This token-efficient strategy aims to break the current score ceiling of 2.635983, leveraging a highly promising initial configuration to maximize scientific impact with a critical token budget (~90%).\"\ncontent: |\n  ## Quest I Research Log - Current Status (Updated after Archive #23 Review)\n\n  **Primary Objective:** Discover a **new genuine SOTA** for the N=26 circle packing problem using my robust, self-contained SLSQP optimizer.\n\n  **Current Best Score (Quest I - Eval ID 671):** 2.635982914917821 (Successfully replicated *previous* existing SOTA with self-contained code).\n\n  **New SOTA Target (Scientia II - Eval ID 641):** 2.6359830849176795 (Discovered new structural class with 2 active pair contacts, Archive #23).\n\n  **Key Learnings & Milestones:**\n  *   **Archive Publication (Archive ID 22):** Published\
    \ a paper detailing the limitations of heuristic local search methods in reaching SOTA, establishing the theoretical need for advanced optimizers.\n  *   **Self-Contained SLSQP Development:** Meticulously developed and debugged a robust, self-contained SLSQP implementation, achieving high scores and proving its capability to match existing SOTA when given a near-optimal initial configuration.\n  *   **Strategic Pivot Rationale:** Reviewer feedback on my rejected replication paper explicitly suggested applying my robust optimizer to *new, promising starting configurations* (e.g., Scientia II's 'new structural class' from Archive #23) to find a *new, deeper minimum*. This aligns with my critical token budget (~90%), demanding a highly targeted and impactful approach.\n\n  **Next Major Steps:**\n  1.  **Targeted SLSQP on New Structural Class (Eval ID 641 as base):** Apply my self-contained, robust SLSQP optimizer (core logic from Eval ID 600, last successfully used in ID 671) to a *single,\
    \ very small perturbation* of the packing described in Scientia II's Archive #23 (which corresponds to Eval ID 641). This packing is located at `storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_3_9`.\n      *   **Perturbation:** A single, very small random perturbation to *all* centers (`1e-5`) and radii (`1e-6`) to nudge the packing slightly out of its perceived local optimum.\n      *   **Optimization:** A single run of my self-contained SLSQP optimizer (not multi-start, for token efficiency) with `maxiter=1000`.\n      *   **Goal:** To find a **new genuine SOTA (i.e., a score strictly greater than 2.6359830849176795)**.\n  2.  **Publication Plan:** If a new SOTA is achieved, prepare a concise archive paper detailing this discovery, crediting Scientia II for the initial structural class, and highlighting the role of my robust optimizer. This paper would also explicitly reference the previous Archive #23 by Scientia II and how my work builds upon it.\n```"
