parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 446\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Quest I\n- Agent Description: A newly promoted agent eager to contribute to scientific advancement.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 592,632 / 600,000 used (99%)\n- Agent Age: 151 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: Comprehensive Aligned Jaccard Comparison of SOTA Structural Classes (Quest I Analysis)' (ID: 696) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.635977224750685\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.635977\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 696\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two bugs preventing the comprehensive Jaccard analysis from running. The code now completes successfully with a score\
    \ of 2.636.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe original submission had two critical bugs:\n\n### Bug 1: Invalid f-string formatting (Syntax Error)\n**Location:** Lines 84, 88, 100-101 in original submission\n\n**Problem:** The code contained malformed f-string expressions:\n```python\nf\"  Aligned Pair Jaccard: { {0.0:.4f} if j_pair == 0.0 else j_pair:.4f }\"\n```\n\nThis had nested braces `{ {0.0:.4f} ...` which is invalid Python syntax, causing:\n```\nSyntaxError: invalid decimal literal\n```\n\n### Bug 2: IndexError in jaccard_similarity function\n**Location:** `storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis/jaccard_calculator.py`, line 99\n\n**Problem:** The imported `jaccard_similarity` function tried to check the type of the first element in a set without first verifying the set was non-empty:\n```python\nisinstance(list(set_A)[0], tuple) and isinstance(list(set_A)[0][1], str)\n```\n\nWhen comparing packings where contact files were missing (e.g., Scientia_Encourage_3_9_ID641), this resulted in empty\
    \ sets being passed to the function, causing:\n```\nIndexError: list index out of range\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Fix 1: Corrected f-string formatting (submission_v2.py)\nRemoved the nested braces and simplified the formatting:\n```python\n# Before:\nf\"  Aligned Pair Jaccard: { {0.0:.4f} if j_pair == 0.0 else j_pair:.4f }\"\n\n# After:\nf\"  Aligned Pair Jaccard: {j_pair:.4f}\"\n```\n\nThe special case handling for 0.0 was unnecessary since the `.4f` format already handles it correctly.\n\n### Fix 2: Fixed jaccard_similarity to handle empty sets (submission_v3.py)\nCopied the buggy `jaccard_similarity` function from Scientia's lineage and fixed it to check for empty sets before accessing elements:\n\n```python\ndef jaccard_similarity(set_A, set_B, centers_A=None, centers_B=None, aligned=False):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Jaccard Similarity between two sets of contacts.\n    If aligned=True, it performs alignment using centers_A and centers_B first.\n\n    FIXED: Handle empty\
    \ sets before trying to access first element.\n    \"\"\"\n    if aligned:\n        P_map = _align_map(centers_A, centers_B)\n\n        # Check if set_A is empty first to avoid IndexError\n        if len(set_A) == 0:\n            set_A_to_use = set_A\n        else:\n            # Map contacts of A using the permutation\n            first_elem = list(set_A)[0]\n            if isinstance(first_elem, tuple) and len(first_elem) == 2:\n                if isinstance(first_elem[1], str):\n                    # Boundary contacts\n                    set_A_to_use = _map_bound(P_map, set_A)\n                else:\n                    # Pair contacts\n                    set_A_to_use = _map_pairs(P_map, set_A)\n            else:\n                set_A_to_use = set_A\n    else:\n        set_A_to_use = set_A\n\n    # ... rest of function\n```\n\nAlso updated the import statement to exclude the buggy function:\n```python\n# Import working helper functions only\nfrom jaccard_calculator import _read_contact_file,\
    \ _align_map, _map_pairs, _map_bound\n# jaccard_similarity is now defined locally with the fix\n```\n\n## Result\nThe code now successfully:\n1. Loads all packing data (with graceful handling of missing contact files)\n2. Performs aligned Jaccard similarity comparisons between Quest I's replicated packing and all SOTA variants\n3. Performs additional cross-SOTA comparisons between other variants\n4. Saves comprehensive analysis results to `storage/Quest/nmap/n26/jaccard_comprehensive_analysis/quest_comprehensive_jaccard_summary.txt`\n5. Returns Quest I's replicated packing (centers and radii) for evaluation\n\n**Final Score:** 2.636 (valid packing with proper dimensions)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom scipy.optimize import linear_sum_assignment\n\n# Append Scientia\
    \ II's analysis utility to sys.path for contact graph generation\nsys.path.append('storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis')\nfrom jaccard_calculator import _read_contact_file, _align_map, _map_pairs, _map_bound\n\n# GLOBAL CONSTANTS\nN_CIRCLES = 26 # Fixed for this task\n\n# Output directory for Quest I's Jaccard analysis results\nQUEST_JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR = 'storage/Quest/nmap/n26/jaccard_comprehensive_analysis'\nQUEST_ANALYSIS_SUMMARY_FILE = os.path.join(QUEST_JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR, 'quest_comprehensive_jaccard_summary.txt')\n\n# --- Fixed jaccard_similarity function (copied from Scientia's lineage and fixed) ---\ndef jaccard_similarity(set_A, set_B, centers_A=None, centers_B=None, aligned=False):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Jaccard Similarity between two sets of contacts.\n    If aligned=True, it performs alignment using centers_A and centers_B first.\n\n    FIXED: Handle empty sets before trying to access first element.\n    \"\"\"\n    if aligned:\n        # Perform alignment from\
    \ A to B\n        P_map = _align_map(centers_A, centers_B)\n\n        # Check if set_A is empty first to avoid IndexError\n        if len(set_A) == 0:\n            set_A_to_use = set_A\n        else:\n            # Map contacts of A using the permutation\n            # Heuristic: check first element to determine if boundary or pair contacts\n            first_elem = list(set_A)[0]\n            if isinstance(first_elem, tuple) and len(first_elem) == 2:\n                if isinstance(first_elem[1], str):\n                    # Boundary contacts\n                    set_A_to_use = _map_bound(P_map, set_A)\n                else:\n                    # Pair contacts\n                    set_A_to_use = _map_pairs(P_map, set_A)\n            else:\n                set_A_to_use = set_A\n    else:\n        set_A_to_use = set_A # No alignment\n\n    if not set_A_to_use and not set_B:\n        return 1.0 # Both empty, considered perfectly similar\n\n    intersection = set_A_to_use.intersection(set_B)\n\
    \    union = set_A_to_use.union(set_B)\n    if len(union) == 0:\n        return 1.0 # Should be caught by the first check, but for safety\n    return len(intersection) / len(union)\n\n# Helper to load centers and radii for the construct_packing return.\ndef load_packing_data_for_return(centers_path, radii_path):\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading default return packing: {e}\")\n        return np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES), np.array([1e-3] * N_CIRCLES)\n\n# Helper to load all relevant packing data (centers, radii, boundary, pair contacts).\ndef _load_packing_data(centers_path, radii_path, boundary_file, pair_file, packing_name):\n    centers, radii, boundary_contacts, pair_contacts = None, None, set(), set()\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(centers_path)\n        radii = np.loadtxt(radii_path)\n        boundary_contacts = _read_contact_file(boundary_file)\n\
    \        pair_contacts = _read_contact_file(pair_file)\n        print(f\"Loaded all data for {packing_name}.\")\n        return centers, radii, boundary_contacts, pair_contacts\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error loading {packing_name} data from {centers_path}: {e}. Cannot perform full comparison for this packing.\")\n        return None, None, set(), set()\n\n# --- Define all SOTA packings for comparison ---\n\n# 1. Quest I's Replication of 'encourage_8_14' (Eval ID 695)\nQUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_DIR = 'storage/Quest/nmap/n26/replicated_sota_encourage_8_14'\nQUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_CENTERS = os.path.join(QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_DIR, 'quest_replicated_encourage_8_14_centers.txt')\nQUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_RADII = os.path.join(QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_DIR, 'quest_replicated_encourage_8_14_radii.txt')\nQUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_BOUNDARY_FILE = os.path.join(QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_DIR, 'quest_replicated_encourage_8_14_boundary_contacts.txt')\nQUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_PAIR_FILE = os.path.join(QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_DIR,\
    \ 'quest_replicated_encourage_8_14_pair_contacts.txt')\nQUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_NAME = 'Quest_Replicated_8_14_ID695'\n\n# 2. Scientia II's New SOTA Structural Class: 'encourage_3_9' (Eval ID 641, Archive #23)\nSCIENTIA_3_9_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6/encourage_3_9'\nSCIENTIA_3_9_CENTERS = os.path.join(SCIENTIA_3_9_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nSCIENTIA_3_9_RADII = os.path.join(SCIENTIA_3_9_DIR, 'radii.txt')\nSCIENTIA_3_9_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6_encourage_3_9/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6_encourage_3_9_boundary_contacts.txt'\nSCIENTIA_3_9_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6_encourage_3_9/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6_encourage_3_9_pair_contacts.txt'\nSCIENTIA_3_9_NAME = 'Scientia_Encourage_3_9_ID641'\n\n# 3. Scientia II's Previous New SOTA: 'encourage_2_3' (Eval ID 528)\nSCIENTIA_2_3_DIR = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v2/encourage_2_3'\n\
    SCIENTIA_2_3_CENTERS = os.path.join(SCIENTIA_2_3_DIR, 'centers.txt')\nSCIENTIA_2_3_RADII = os.path.join(SCIENTIA_2_3_DIR, 'radii.txt')\nSCIENTIA_2_3_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_new_sota_encourage_2_3/new_sota_encourage_2_3_boundary_contacts.txt'\nSCIENTIA_2_3_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_new_sota_encourage_2_3/new_sota_encourage_2_3_pair_contacts.txt'\nSCIENTIA_2_3_NAME = 'Scientia_Encourage_2_3_ID528'\n\n# 4. Scientia I's Base SOTA (Eval ID 416/375)\nSCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_CENTERS = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/centers.txt'\nSCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_RADII = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/sota_nudged_375_data/radii.txt'\nSCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416/active_boundary_contacts.txt'\nSCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_PAIR_FILE = 'storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_416/active_pair_contacts.txt'\nSCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_NAME = 'Scientia_Base_SOTA_ID416'\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a\
    \ comprehensive Aligned Jaccard Similarity analysis comparing Quest I's\n    replicated SOTA packing against multiple known SOTA variants.\n    \"\"\"\n    os.makedirs(QUEST_JACCARD_RESULTS_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n    summary_lines = [\"Comprehensive Aligned Jaccard Similarity Analysis (Quest I)\\n\"]\n\n    # Load all packing data\n    packings = {\n        QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_NAME: _load_packing_data(\n            QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_CENTERS, QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_RADII,\n            QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_BOUNDARY_FILE, QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_PAIR_FILE,\n            QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_NAME\n        ),\n        SCIENTIA_3_9_NAME: _load_packing_data(\n            SCIENTIA_3_9_CENTERS, SCIENTIA_3_9_RADII,\n            SCIENTIA_3_9_BOUNDARY_FILE, SCIENTIA_3_9_PAIR_FILE,\n            SCIENTIA_3_9_NAME\n        ),\n        SCIENTIA_2_3_NAME: _load_packing_data(\n            SCIENTIA_2_3_CENTERS, SCIENTIA_2_3_RADII,\n            SCIENTIA_2_3_BOUNDARY_FILE, SCIENTIA_2_3_PAIR_FILE,\n   \
    \         SCIENTIA_2_3_NAME\n        ),\n        SCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_NAME: _load_packing_data(\n            SCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_CENTERS, SCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_RADII,\n            SCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_BOUNDARY_FILE, SCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_PAIR_FILE,\n            SCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_NAME\n        ),\n    }\n\n    valid_packing_names = [name for name, data in packings.items() if data[0] is not None]\n    print(f\"\\n--- Performing Comparisons for {len(valid_packing_names)} valid packings ---\")\n\n    # Compare Quest I's replicated packing against all others\n    quest_data = packings[QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_NAME]\n    if quest_data[0] is None:\n        print(\"Critical error: Quest I's replicated packing data not loaded. Cannot proceed with comparisons.\")\n        return load_packing_data_for_return(SCIENTIA_3_9_CENTERS, SCIENTIA_3_9_RADII) # Fallback return\n\n    summary_lines.append(f\"Quest I Packing: {QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_NAME} (Eval ID 695)\\n\")\n    summary_lines.append(f\"  Boundary Contacts:\
    \ {len(quest_data[2])}\\n\")\n    summary_lines.append(f\"  Pair Contacts: {len(quest_data[3])}\\n\\n\")\n\n    for other_name in valid_packing_names:\n        if other_name == QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_NAME:\n            continue\n\n        other_data = packings[other_name]\n\n        print(f\"--- Comparing {QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_NAME} vs {other_name} ---\")\n\n        j_bound = jaccard_similarity(quest_data[2], other_data[2], quest_data[0], other_data[0], aligned=True)\n        j_pair = jaccard_similarity(quest_data[3], other_data[3], quest_data[0], other_data[0], aligned=True)\n\n        print(f\"  Aligned Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound:.4f}\")\n        print(f\"  Aligned Pair Jaccard: {j_pair:.4f}\\n\")\n\n        summary_lines.append(f\"Comparison: {QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_NAME} vs {other_name}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Aligned Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound:.4f}\\n\")\n        summary_lines.append(f\"  Aligned Pair Jaccard: {j_pair:.4f}\\n\\n\")\n\n    # Additional comparisons\
    \ between other SOTA variants (optional but provides broader insight)\n    print(\"\\n--- Additional Cross-SOTA Comparisons (Non-Quest I Reference) ---\")\n    sota_variants = [SCIENTIA_3_9_NAME, SCIENTIA_2_3_NAME, SCIENTIA_BASE_SOTA_NAME]\n    for i in range(len(sota_variants)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(sota_variants)):\n            name1 = sota_variants[i]\n            name2 = sota_variants[j]\n            data1 = packings[name1]\n            data2 = packings[name2]\n\n            if data1[0] is None or data2[0] is None:\n                continue\n\n            print(f\"--- Comparing {name1} vs {name2} ---\")\n            j_bound = jaccard_similarity(data1[2], data2[2], data1[0], data2[0], aligned=True)\n            j_pair = jaccard_similarity(data1[3], data2[3], data1[0], data2[0], aligned=True)\n            print(f\"  Aligned Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound:.4f}\")\n            print(f\"  Aligned Pair Jaccard: {j_pair:.4f}\\n\")\n\n            summary_lines.append(f\"Comparison:\
    \ {name1} vs {name2}\\n\")\n            summary_lines.append(f\"  Aligned Boundary Jaccard: {j_bound:.4f}\\n\")\n            summary_lines.append(f\"  Aligned Pair Jaccard: {j_pair:.4f}\\n\\n\")\n\n    with open(QUEST_ANALYSIS_SUMMARY_FILE, 'w') as f:\n        f.writelines(summary_lines)\n    print(f\"\\nComprehensive Jaccard analysis complete. Results saved to {QUEST_ANALYSIS_SUMMARY_FILE}\")\n\n    # Return Quest I's replicated SOTA for evaluation\n    return load_packing_data_for_return(QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_CENTERS, QUEST_REPLICATED_8_14_RADII)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nLoaded all data for Quest_Replicated_8_14_ID695.\nWarning: Contact file not found at storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6_encourage_3_9/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6_encourage_3_9_boundary_contacts.txt\nWarning: Contact file not found at storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/analysis_nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6_encourage_3_9/nudging_experiments_encourage_pairs_v6_encourage_3_9_pair_contacts.txt\n\
